## What remains before the platform goal is complete

1. Reconcile the divergent Multi-Agent-Memory branches and establish one exact public release URL, revision, immutable package, target profile, tag policy, deployment receipt, and full-site byte verification.
2. Qualify LocalEndpoints.com and RemoteEndpoints.com on a supported production runtime with target-bound atomic activation. Publish honest dated/versioned release ledgers only from independently accepted evidence.
3. Freeze the complete Connect tree, close its package dependency graph, build and production-sign Connect plus both plugins, install exact reviewed bytes on clean Windows systems, and prove installed/source/package identity.
4. Prove the unattended Remote lifecycle on owned fixtures: install, enable, pair once, outbound reconnect, select computer, receive fresh timestamped pictures, send an arbitrary prompt, execute with real local Windows authority, observe progress/results/errors/receipts, and exercise Stop, Pause, Disable, rotation, Revoke, expiry, duplication, stale state, interruption, locked-session, UAC, and network-recovery boundaries without private leakage.
5. Prove the Memory swarm on two independently installed Connect instances: two distinct active names and memories work concurrently; duplicate normalized name loses; the same immutable memory cannot gain a second writer across path/computer changes; a true branch gets a new identity and complete lineage; renewal, expiry, takeover, reconnect, restart, and every stale mutation fail with deterministic receipts and no side effects.
6. Prove authenticated UI and Demo parity through the same renderers, controls, validation, and client methods, with unmistakable session-local mock data, clean scene routes, accessible overlays, screenshots, keyboard/reduced-motion/forced-colors behavior, narrow-screen reflow, privacy containment, and guarded zero-protected-request assertions.
7. Recheck SEO, canonical URLs, structured data, crawler files, OpenAPI, manifests, route inventory, release logs, package/download trust copy, and public claims across all sites so every surface describes the same verified architecture and every remaining unknown is visibly labeled.

## Cold-start continuation sequence

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, this file, `.uai/startup-packet.uai`, and every file in its declared order; inspect active handoff buckets before broad work.
2. Run `git status`, resolve the authoritative root and branch, fetch current refs read-only, and compare current bytes with the newest exact independent report. Preserve all other agents' and human changes.
3. Query the current public version, release, health, Demo, and contract routes. Record SOURCE, PACKAGE, INSTALLED, DEPLOYMENT, and LIVE independently.
4. Search the shared Improvement handoff for the newest report for the exact subsystem and gate. Treat older source packages and synthetic/debug artifacts as historical evidence only.
5. When authenticated MemoryEndpoints coordination is available, check current-message and project rooms, acknowledge handled notifications, use a unique agent identity, and acquire the required project/path or writer lease before shared mutation. If it is unavailable, continue from local `.uai` and public-safe handoff evidence without requesting or exposing a credential.
6. Prefer implementation and direct verification over another design memo. Stop at the first failed release gate, preserve exact public-safe evidence, remediate the owning source cleanly, and rerun from fresh frozen bytes.

## Required Next Prompt

### Feature/improvement focus

Continue the world-class unattended RemoteEndpoints, LocalEndpoints Connect, and MemoryEndpoints integration from the first unclosed gate above. Preserve one-time standing remote authority, exact authenticated/Demo UI parity, full plugin power, unique swarm names, exclusive immutable-memory writers, and true concurrent branches without legacy support or claim inflation.

### Code/source changes

Reconcile the authoritative source and contract before modifying code. Implement the smallest complete vertical slice in its owning repository, update every dogfood consumer to the one current contract, remove superseded behavior in the same change, and keep credentials, private payloads, pictures, identifiers, packages, and deployment evidence out of public source.

### Automated tests/checks

Run focused tests first, then each owning repository's complete source, lint, build, browser, accessibility, privacy, package, signing, installed-byte, deployment-receipt, and live-revision gates required by the changed slice. Obtain independent SOURCE, PACKAGE, INSTALLED, DEPLOYMENT, and LIVE verdicts separately and never promote a partial GO into platform completion.
